  "hypotheses": {
    "H1_primary": "On the R0-wrong pairs, COISC improves closed-loop tracking over R0: unit = pair, effect = family-equal mean over 24 plants of MAE[COISC] - MAE[R0]; supported iff every pair is evaluable and the 95% percentile bootstrap CI upper bound (20,000 draws over pairs, seed 20261105) is < 0.",
    "H2_primary": "On all other seed-scenario pairs, COISC is non-inferior to R0: unit = seed, effect = mean over that seed's non-R0-wrong scenarios of the family-equal mean over the 6 panel-B plants of MAE[COISC] - MAE[R0]; supported iff all 40 seeds are evaluable and the 95% bootstrap CI upper bound (over seeds) is < 0.10 C.",
    "verdict": "SUPPORTED iff H1 and H2 are both supported; otherwise PARTIAL_H1_ONLY, PARTIAL_H2_ONLY or NOT_SUPPORTED. The verdict is reported whatever it is.",
    "margin_justification": "0.10 C is about 5% of the mean closed-loop MAE_track of R0 on this bench (1.95 C over the 13 earlier seeds); it is fixed a priori as a small fraction of the bench MAE, before any closed-loop run of these 40 seeds. No physical tolerance is claimed for it."
  },
